                      "title":  "Technology",
                      "text":  "The Edison Township Public Schools Department of Technology supports teaching, learning, communication, and district operations through the effective, secure, and responsible use of technology.\nWorking collaboratively with schools and departments, the Technology Department provides leadership and support for the digital tools, systems, infrastructure, and devices that help students and staff learn, connect, create, and communicate.\nOur goal is to ensure that students are prepared to use technology responsibly, ethically, and effectively in an evolving digital world. Students are encouraged to develop the skills necessary to access, evaluate, analyze, create, and communicate information while practicing strong digital citizenship and responsible use of emerging technologies.\nThe Technology Department supports district technology infrastructure and services, including Internet connectivity, wireless networking, information systems, servers, communication systems, instructional technology, district-issued devices, Google Workspace for Education, and other applications and cloud-based services used throughout Edison Township Public Schools.\nSupport Hours: 8am-4pm Monday through Friday\nTechnology Helpdesk Ticket - Please click here .\nTo email the Helpdesk: Email Help Desk\nTo call the Helpdesk: 732.452.4998 or internally @ x24998",
